{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"review\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Semantic review of the artifact that adds the applied-state observation to claim C1-recovery-adopts-committed-vector (artifact 05dc6a3632954371911663108e7e18e8, executed as 2f186bc17e13432fae3b653b42e46941). The retained run reproduces the observation (peer_value 04 against recoverer_value and third_value (void), applied_match false), but the property asserts something the accepted claim's scope explicitly excludes, so the item is recorded as revision_needed with scope as the challenged component.\\\",\n \\\"artifact_id\\\":\\\"05dc6a3632954371911663108e7e18e8\\\",\n \\\"review_items\\\":[{\n  \\\"aspect\\\":\\\"checker_correspondence\\\",\n  \\\"status\\\":\\\"revision_needed\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S20-exec\\\",\\\"S23-state-conflict-apply\\\",\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\",\\\"S14-recovery-start-prepare\\\"],\n  \\\"report_title\\\":\\\"应用层不一致属性超出已接受义务范围\\\",\n  \\\"report_answer\\\":\\\"运行结果本身可复现：对端状态机读到 04，恢复者与第三副本读到 (void)，applied_match=false，即已提交记录的不一致确实进入了状态机。但已接受的义务 C1 在其 scope.excluded 中明确排除了 execution of the instance and client-visible replies，因此该属性断言的是范围之外事项，不能用来确认 C1；它需要作为独立义务（或经 F2/F3 扩展范围）重新固定。\\\",\n  \\\"challenged_components\\\":[\\\"scope\\\"],\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Requirement versus predicate: the accepted claim requires that a reply reporting the instance COMMITTED be adopted; the added property instead asserts that, after each replica applies the instance it holds committed, the state machines agree on the instance's key. The observation is a consequence of the requirement rather than the requirement's own premise, and the accepted claim's scope list names exactly that consequence as excluded (execution of the instance and client-visible replies). Entry and observation: the harness applies each record with Exec.executeCommand directly and probes the store with a GET command, which is a declared substitution (the production executeCommands loop, watermark advancement and the recovery timeout are not exercised); the records' COMMITTED status is by construction, and the three values printed in the event are read from the replicated store rather than derived from a context expected to change. Oracle and identity: comparing the three printed values for one instance and one key is a fair encoding of applied-state agreement, and the instance identity is shared with the prerequisite reply, so the failure is not an artefact of correlation. Contrary evidence and the reason for the negative judgment: the element that conflicts is the claim's own excluded list, which the source of record for the accepted obligation states; a consequence outside that scope can still be true and valuable, but confirming it under this claim would treat an independent limit as a confirmation gate, so the artifact should either drop the applied-state property or the proposition should be fixed as its own obligation whose scope includes applying the instance to the state machine. The rest of the artifact (the correction that drives every queued round and re-reads InstanceSpace) reproduces the earlier reviewed findings and does not itself change them.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"the accepted claim C1-recovery-adopts-committed-vector lists execution of the instance and client-visible replies under scope.excluded, so the applied-state property tests outside the accepted proposition (claim C1 scope, S20-exec)\\\",\n    \\\"the event is reproducible in the retained stream (applied_state_divergence with peer_value 04 and recoverer_value (void)), so the objection is about scope and attribution rather than about the observation (check 2f186bc17e13432fae3b653b42e46941)\\\"],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"the applied-state observation remains useful as construction knowledge and can be re-used by a new obligation whose scope includes applying the instance\\\",\n   \\\"the harness invokes Exec.executeCommand directly, so scheduling, watermarks and the recovery timeout are outside even the substituted execution path\\\",\n   \\\"the earlier artifacts and their reviews are unaffected; this review concerns only the artifact that adds the applied-state property\\\"]}]}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-review-applied.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-review-applied.json 2>&1 | head -14\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
